      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bly%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Bly is the site of the only fatalities in the contiguous United States during World War Two.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bly%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A Japanese Fu-Go balloon bomb exploded on May 5, 1945, as curious picnickers pulled it from the woods near Bly.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bly%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The OC and E Woods Line State Trail passes through Bly, tracing the old railbeds of the Oregon, California and Eastern Railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
